# Slide Title Centering

When slide titles (especially gradient-text headings) appear off-center, avoid relying on `text-center` or `mx-auto` with `inline-block` — they can be unreliable with `background-clip: text` and gradient styles.

## Use flex containers for centering

Wrap the title in a flex container with `items-center`:

```jsx
<div className="flex flex-col items-center text-center">
  <h2 className="fctg-heading ...">Title text</h2>
  <p className="fctg-subtitle mt-1">Subtitle</p>
</div>
```

Or center the whole section:

```jsx
<div className="flex flex-col items-center">
  <div className="flex flex-col items-center text-center max-w-md">
    <h2 className="fctg-heading ...">Title</h2>
    <p className="fctg-subtitle mt-1">Subtitle</p>
  </div>
</div>
```

`flex flex-col items-center` reliably centers children horizontally regardless of gradient/background-clip styles.
